WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.020
Now apply the same design process to a bookstore
Start by identifying

00:00:06.046 --> 00:00:12.539
candidate entities such as customer book author
order and order item Then

00:00:12.566 --> 00:00:18.097
define one-row grain for each table Think about the
relationships

00:00:19.021 --> 00:00:24.416
One customer can place many orders One order can
contain many books

00:00:25.337 --> 00:00:32.090
One book can have several authors which suggests
another many-to-many relationship Choose

00:00:32.117 --> 00:00:36.617
stable primary keys and protect important natural
identifiers such as email or

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:42.302
ISBN when appropriate Before revealing the sample
direction create

00:00:42.328 --> 00:00:47.447
your own simple design first There can be more than
one reasonable

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:51.500
implementation but every table should have a clear
grain and every relationship

00:00:51.526 --> 00:00:53.434
should be explainable in plain language
